# MICRO-PURCHASE OUTREACH — THE DIRECT SALES PIPELINE

**Micro-purchases are DDI's fastest path to revenue. No formal bids. No lengthy proposals. A contracting officer can call you and place an order TODAY if you're on their radar. This rule governs how NEXUS handles micro-purchase outreach.**

---

## WHAT IS A MICRO-PURCHASE?

| Threshold | Type | What It Means |
|---|---|---|
| **Under $10,000** | Federal Micro-Purchase | CO can buy from ANY vendor without competition. Just a credit card swipe. |
| **$10,000–$250,000** | Simplified Acquisition | Requires 3 quotes, but EDWOSB sole-source eligible up to $7M bypasses this. |
| **BPA (Blanket Purchase Agreement)** | Standing Order | Once you're on a BPA, they call you repeatedly. Recurring revenue. |

**DDI's EDWOSB status means a CO can sole-source up to $7M to DDI without competition. Micro-purchase outreach is about getting on their radar so they USE that authority.**

