## OUTREACH PROTOCOL — EMAIL FIRST, CALL WARM LEADS

**Volume target: 50 contacts per week. Email is the first touch. Phone calls are for respondents.**

### The Sequence (Every Contact, Every Time)

```
1. EMAIL FIRST (batch 50 per week)
   → Use the sector email template
   → Replace [Name] with contact name (or "Dear [Title]" if name unknown)
   → Attach sector-specific capability statement (v3 format, PDF)
   → Subject line MUST include CAGE 8UMX3
   → UPDATE NEXUS immediately after sending

2. WAIT FOR REPLIES (5 business days)
   → Monitor inbox for responses
   → Any reply = WARM LEAD → move to step 3

3. CALL WARM LEADS (respondents only)
   → Use the sector phone script
   → Reference your email: "I sent over our capability statement last week..."
   → Goal: schedule a 15-minute call or get added to vendor list
   → UPDATE NEXUS with call outcome

4. FOLLOW UP non-respondents (after 5 business days)
   → One follow-up email referencing prior contact
   → If no response after follow-up → move to NEXT BATCH
   → Do NOT call cold non-respondents — they'll remember the email when they need you

5. REPEAT weekly
   → 50 new contacts per week
   → Follow up on prior week's non-respondents
   → Call any new warm leads from prior batches
```

### Weekly Cadence

| Day | Action | Volume |
|---|---|---|
| **Monday** | Send new batch of emails (50 contacts) | 50 |
| **Tuesday** | Send follow-ups to prior week's non-respondents | 20-40 |
| **Wednesday–Thursday** | Call warm leads who replied | 5-15 |
| **Friday** | Update NEXUS, prep next week's batch | — |

### Email Subject Line Format

```
CAGE 8UMX3 | [Service Description] | EDWOSB | [Agency/Installation Name]
```

**Examples:**
- `CAGE 8UMX3 | Fingerprinting & Credentialing Services | EDWOSB | Selfridge ANGB`
- `CAGE 8UMX3 | FTA-Compliant C/TPA | 5,100+ Collection Sites | EDWOSB | SMART`
- `CAGE 8UMX3 | EDWOSB Emergency Logistics Contractor | TWIC-Credentialed | MSP/EMHSD`

### Capability Statement Rules

- ALWAYS attach a cap statement to every email
- Use the CORRECT sector version (fingerprinting = green, drug testing = blue/red, etc.)
- Must be v3 format (see `cap-statement-v3-enforcement.mdc`)
- If a contact serves dual sectors (e.g., VA = fingerprinting + NEMT), use the primary sector cap statement and mention the second service in the email body

